1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-1--1c-begin-comprehension","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-1/1c-begin-comprehension","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-1/1c-begin-comprehension","sourceHash":"184b2874e2238a51c6dc36dfaa5e88250007101393f6e3e936ad0d0e3500e023","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:39.925Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"1C — Begin Comprehension","zh":"1C——开始培养理解能力"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The most common 1000 words in a language make up about 70% of everything in that language. These words are absolutely everywhere, and you need to become very familiar with them before you can understand anything deeper.","zh":"一门语言中最常见的1000个词，大约构成该语言全部内容的70%。这些词无处不在；在你理解更深层的内容之前，必须先对它们非常熟悉。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>The rest of Phase 1 is devoted to learning those words</strong> and practicing real comprehension.","zh":"<strong>第一阶段的其余部分都 devoted 于学习这些词</strong>，并练习真正的理解能力。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Until now, you've been noticing patterns and picking up basics. Now you're going to start actually piecing together meaning from real content.","zh":"到目前为止，你一直在留意规律、掌握基础。现在，你将开始真正从真实内容中拼凑出意义。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your priming continues (you're still learning vocab every day), but the big shift is in your immersion. You're moving beyond just noticing — you're starting to <em>understand</em>.","zh":"你的预热学习仍在继续（你每天还在学习词汇），但最大的变化在于你的沉浸方式。你不再只是留意——而是开始<em>理解</em>。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Interactive Reading with Audio</strong> — This is the core immersion activity for this sub-phase. You watch or read something in your target language and actively work to understand it: pausing, looking things up in a dictionary, replaying sections. It's slow at first, and that's fine. You're training the skill of extracting meaning from real content, which is fundamentally different from studying flashcards. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/interactive-reading-with-audio\">Interactive Reading with Audio</a>","zh":"<strong>带音频的互动阅读</strong>——这是本子阶段的核心沉浸活动。你观看或阅读目标语言内容，并主动努力去理解：暂停、查词典、重播片段。刚开始会很慢，这没关系。你正在训练从真实内容中提取意义的能力，而这与学习闪卡有着根本区别。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/interactive-reading-with-audio\">带音频的互动阅读</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You'll need content that's challenging but not impossible. There are several techniques that help with this:","zh":"你需要选择有挑战性但并非不可能理解的内容。有几种技巧可以帮助你做到这一点："}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>The Multipass Method</strong> — Instead of using content once and moving on, you go through the same material multiple times with different approaches. First you might read through slowly with lookups, then watch again without pausing, then listen to just the audio later. Each pass lets you pick up more, and the familiarity makes difficult content accessible. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-multipass-method\">The Multipass Method</a>","zh":"<strong>多遍学习法</strong>——不要只使用一次内容就继续往下，而是用不同方式多次处理同一份材料。第一遍可以慢慢阅读并查词，接着再看一遍但不暂停，之后再单独听音频。每一遍都会让你多理解一些，而熟悉感也会让原本困难的内容变得可以接近。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-multipass-method\">多遍学习法</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Re-experiencing Content</strong> — Revisiting things you already know in your target language. Watching a dubbed version of a favorite show, reading a translated book you've read before. Your existing knowledge of the story acts as scaffolding, letting you understand far more than you otherwise would at this level. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/re-experiencing-content\">Re-experiencing Content</a>","zh":"<strong>重新体验内容</strong>——用目标语言重访你已经了解的内容，比如观看喜欢的剧集的配音版，或阅读一本以前读过的译作。你对故事已有的了解会发挥支架作用，让你在当前水平下理解远超平时的内容。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/re-experiencing-content\">重新体验内容</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Hybrid Immersion Content</strong> — At this stage, you'll be using content that combines text and audio together, like TV shows with subtitles or YouTube videos with captions. Having both channels available lets you use your developing reading ability to support your listening, making the content much more accessible than audio or text alone. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/hybrid-immersion-content\">Hybrid Immersion Content</a>","zh":"<strong>混合式沉浸内容</strong>——在这个阶段，你会使用同时结合文字和音频的内容，例如带字幕的电视剧或带字幕的 YouTube 视频。两个通道都可用时，你可以用正在发展的阅读能力来支持听力，因此内容会比只有音频或文字时更容易理解。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/hybrid-immersion-content\">混合式沉浸内容</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Character Study (for applicable languages)</strong> — If your target language uses a character-based writing system (Chinese, Japanese), this is when you may start learning characters alongside your other study. This is not relevant for most languages. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/character-study\">Character Study</a>","zh":"<strong>文字研究（适用于相关语言）</strong>——如果你的目标语言使用以汉字为基础的书写系统（中文、日语），现在可以开始在其他学习内容之外学习文字。这对大多数语言并不适用。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/character-study\">文字研究</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The balance shifts toward more immersion time now that you have enough vocabulary to start understanding:","zh":"现在你已经拥有足够的词汇，可以开始理解内容，因此学习时间的分配会更多地转向沉浸："}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 30%","zh":"<strong>预热学习：</strong>30%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 70%","zh":"<strong>互动沉浸：</strong>70%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 20 mins","zh":"词汇学习：20分钟"},{"en":"Interactive Reading with Audio (comprehensible input): 20 mins","zh":"带音频的互动阅读（可理解输入）：20分钟"},{"en":"Interactive Reading with Audio (dubbed familiar show): 20 mins","zh":"带音频的互动阅读（熟悉剧集的配音版）：20分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to 1D when you:","zh":"当你满足以下条件时，进入1D："}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Can understand many basic sentences without looking anything up <ul><li><em>Examples: \"How are you?\" \"And he did too.\" \"That looks good.\"</em></li></ul>","zh":"无需查任何内容，就能理解许多基础句子 <ul><li><em>示例：“你好吗？”“他也做了。”“看起来不错。”</em></li></ul>"},{"en":"Can understand many non-complex sentences with the help of tools <ul><li><em>Examples: \"We're going to the market.\" \"Today, we're going to talk about cheese.\"</em></li></ul>","zh":"借助工具，能理解许多不复杂的句子 <ul><li><em>示例：“我们要去市场。”“今天我们要谈谈奶酪。”</em></li></ul>"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0024","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Reading-while-listening (with subtitles or captions) outperforms either modality alone, as shown by Webb &amp; Chang (2015). When you read text and hear audio simultaneously, you're leveraging two channels to extract meaning, and the combination allows you to understand content that would be too difficult using only listening or reading alone. This is why the Multipass Method works: familiarity from the first pass makes the second pass with a single modality accessible.","zh":"Webb 和 Chang（2015）的研究表明，边阅读边听（配合字幕或文字稿）优于单独使用其中任何一种方式。同时阅读文字并听音频时，你是在利用两个通道提取意义；两者结合后，可以理解仅靠听或仅靠读会过于困难的内容。这正是多遍学习法有效的原因：第一遍建立的熟悉感，会让第二遍使用单一通道时变得可理解。"}},{"id":"segment-0025","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Re-experiencing familiar content is powerful because you're not starting from zero — your existing knowledge of the story acts as comprehensible input scaffolding. You understand the narrative structure, the plot beats, and the character motivations, which lets your brain focus its limited language processing capacity on the words and grammar themselves rather than trying to figure out what's happening.","zh":"重新体验熟悉内容之所以有效，是因为你并非从零开始——你对故事已有的了解会充当可理解输入的支架。你理解叙事结构、情节发展和人物动机，这让大脑可以把有限的语言处理能力集中在词汇和语法本身，而不是先弄清楚发生了什么。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
